{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is hyperedge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", with an edge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{i, n + p}"},{"type":"text","text":" for each incidence. It is bipartite and simple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices on the left, hyperedges on the right), an empty hyperedge is an isolated vertex, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it loses nothing."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","text":"Hypergraph"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Edge position ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"text":" is incidence number ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"text":": the incidences hyperedge by hyperedge, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index order, and within a hyperedge in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices"},{"text":" order. So ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedEdge(i, n + p)"},{"text":", the rows of the hyperedge side are contiguous ranges, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array (a weight of a vertex in a hyperedge) is indexed by edge position. A view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a snapshot, so its own positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until its next mutation: the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"text":", inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one), and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array must be rebuilt for it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LabeledGraph law."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Every index member reads the base’s rows:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shifted by n, and of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is ","type":"text"},{"code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". So ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traversal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Connectivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ShortestPaths","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the rest run on the view without hashing a vertex. ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withIncidentIndexRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes the view’s rows out once per call from the base’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withIncidenceRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(n + m + p), so whole-graph algorithms (components, bridges, cut vertices) run at an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adjacency-list copy’s speed on every base.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Costs.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The view keeps each hyperedge’s first incidence number, so a hyperedge’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a range, O(1). On ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which stores its incidences,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every read is O(1) plus the row. On any other base, ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"binary-search the hyperedge and find the member by its rank (","type":"text"},{"code":"_memberIndex(atRank:…)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and O(log m + k) by default, and a vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" finds its place in each of its hyperedges: O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which counts bits, and O(Σ k) over them on a base without a faster ","type":"text"},{"code":"_memberRank","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BipartiteGraph(h.incidenceGraph, left: 0 ..< h.vertexCount)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the bipartite structure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the view’s components restricted to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n"},{"type":"text","text":" are the hypergraph’s."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview"]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView.swift#L50","fileName":"IncidenceGraphView.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:11Hypergraphs18IncidenceGraphViewV","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"}],"modules":[{"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"role":"symbol","title":"IncidenceGraphView","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Edges-swift.struct","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/IncidentEdgeIndices","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Neighbors"],"title":"Structures","generated":true},{"anchor":"I